 "news": {
  "date": "2026-09-16",
  "asof": "2026-09-17 20:01 UTC",
  "headline": "The Fed hiked for the first time since 2023 \u2014 and the Dow took it three times harder than the Nasdaq",
  "standfirst": "Twenty-five basis points to 3.75-4.00%, unanimous, with the statement dropping the three dissents it carried last time because it gave them what they wanted. The dot plot has twelve of eighteen members projecting one more hike this year. Stocks were higher at 2pm and then fell through Warsh\u2019s press conference \u2014 the Dow down more than 700 points while he spoke, closing \u22121.15% against the S&P\u2019s 0.44% and a flat Nasdaq. That split is the session: the market marked down the economy, not the discount rate. The ten-year held above 5%. Crude fell for the first time since the pipeline was cut, to about $102.40, after Aramco said it can restore half the line within days. In the book nothing closed, nothing came near a stop, and the best performer was PLTR at +1.03%. Heat 3.05R against 3.0R.",
  "themes": [
   {
    "kicker": "What's next",
    "right": "BoJ and triple witching, Friday, same session",
    "title": "The decision is behind us; the harder one lands on the quarter's largest expiry",
